# 2. RED TEAM MASTER CONCEPT

A red team simulates realistic adversary behavior to evaluate an organization's security.

Simplified:

```text
OBJECTIVE
   ↓
RECON
   ↓
ENUMERATION
   ↓
INITIAL ACCESS
   ↓
EXPLOITATION
   ↓
PRIVILEGE ESCALATION
   ↓
LATERAL MOVEMENT
   ↓
OBJECTIVE
   ↓
REPORT
```

---

# 3. IMPORTANT DISTINCTION

Red teaming is not simply:

> "Hack everything."

It is:

> **An authorized, objective-driven security assessment designed to test people, processes and technology.**

---

# 4. RED TEAM VS PENTEST

| Penetration Test | Red Team |
|---|---|
| Usually vulnerability-focused | Objective/adversary-focused |
| Often broader technical testing | Simulates realistic adversary behavior |
| Defined scope | Often objective-driven |
| Finds vulnerabilities | Tests attack paths and defenses |
| Shorter engagement | May involve longer scenarios |
| Technical focus | People + process + technology |

---

# 5. RED TEAM VS PURPLE TEAM

### Red Team

Simulates attacker behavior.

### Blue Team

Defends and detects.

### Purple Team

Combines both teams to improve detection and defense.

```text
RED
 ↓
ATTACK SIMULATION
 ↓
BLUE
 ↓
DETECTION
 ↓
PURPLE
 ↓
IMPROVEMENT
```

